# ==============================================================================
# Temperature Ramp Snippet (linear heating/cooling with fix nvt)
# Apply when: annealing, melting, or equilibrating across a temperature window
# ==============================================================================
# USAGE:
# - fix nvt temp Tstart Tstop Tdamp ramps the target temperature LINEARLY from
#   Tstart to Tstop over the following `run`.
# - Ramp rate = (Tstop - Tstart) / (run steps x timestep). Keep it gentle:
#   a typical rate is 0.1-1 K/ps; please adjust to your system size.
#   Example: 300 -> 600 K over 300 ps  = 1 K/ps  (units metal: run 300000 at 0.001 ps)
# - For production at the final temperature, follow with a second run whose
#   Tstart == Tstop.

fix             ramp all nvt temp 300.0 600.0 0.1
run             300000          # 300 ps at 1 fs -> 1 K/ps heating
unfix           ramp

# --- production block at the final temperature ---
# fix           prod all nvt temp 600.0 600.0 0.1
# run           200000
